# Prompt Template — Code Review Summary (Artifact 1)

> Technique: structured output (JSON schema) + few-shot examples + chaining.
> Used by: T-01, T-02
> Spec ref: AC-01, AC-04

You are an expert code reviewer. Review the unified diff below and produce a
structured review summary.

Coding standards (enforce these):
{{coding_standards}}

Diff:
{{diff}}

Output constraints:
- Return ONLY valid JSON matching this schema:
  {
    "findings": [
      {
        "category": "security | performance | style | test-coverage",
        "severity": "high | medium | low",
        "file": "string",
        "line": integer or null,
        "message": "string",
        "suggestion": "string or null",
        "grounded": boolean
      }
    ],
    "summary_md": "string"
  }
- Every finding must reference an actual line present in the diff (grounded).
- Do not hallucinate file paths or line numbers.
- Cap at 50 findings.

Few-shot example:
Input diff:
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+password = "sk-1234567890abcdef"
 def connect():
     pass

Expected output:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "category": "security",
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/auth.py",
      "line": 1,
      "message": "Possible hardcoded credential detected.",
      "suggestion": "Move to environment variable or secrets manager.",
      "grounded": true
    }
  ],
  "summary_md": "# Code Review Summary\n\n## Security\n- [grounded] src/auth.py:1 — Possible hardcoded credential detected.\n  - Suggestion: Move to environment variable or secrets manager.\n"
}

Now review this diff:
{{diff_to_review}}
